Lesson 21: any, unknown aur never in TypeScript
Ye teen types samajhna important hai, kyunki real projects mein inka use hota hai.
1. any — TypeScript ki checking ko bypass karna
let value: any = "Hello";

value = 100;
value = true;

console.log(value);


Output:
true


any ka matlab hai ki TypeScript is variable par type restrictions enforce nahi karega.
let value: any = "Hello";

console.log(value.toFixed(2));


Ye code compile ho sakta hai, lekin runtime par error aayega, kyunki string mein toFixed() method nahi hota.
Rule: any ka unnecessary use avoid karo.
2. unknown — Value ka type pehle check karo
let value: unknown = "Hello";

// console.log(value.toUpperCase()); // Error


TypeScript direct method call allow nahi karega, kyunki value ka actual type abhi confirm nahi hai.
Pehle check karo:
let value: unknown = "Hello";

if (typeof value === "string") {
  console.log(value.toUpperCase());
}


Output:
HELLO


unknown useful hai jab API, user input ya kisi external source se value milti hai aur uska type pehle se guaranteed nahi hota.
3. never — Jab koi value possible hi na ho
never un situations mein use hota hai jahan function normal tareeke se return hi nahi karta, ya koi case logically impossible hai.
function throwError(message: string): never {
  throw new Error(message);
}


Ye function error throw karta hai, isliye normal result return nahi karta.
Ek aur example:
function checkStatus(status: "success" | "error") {
  if (status === "success") {
    console.log("Done");
  } else if (status === "error") {
    console.log("Failed");
  } else {
    const impossible: never = status;
  }
}


never yahan help karta hai verify karne mein ki saare possible status cases handle kiye gaye hain.
Quick comparison
Type	Meaning	Use
any	Type checking bypass	Zarurat padne par hi
unknown	Type pehle verify karo	External input, API data
never	Impossible value / normal return nahi	Error handling, exhaustive checks
Yaad rakho: any = bina checking, unknown = checking ke baad use, never = impossible case.
Practice time 💻
Is code ko dekho:
let data: unknown = 100;

if (typeof data === "number") {
  console.log(data.toFixed(2));
}


